Title: NIGHT FERRY
Credit: Written by
Author: Sam Rivera
Draft date: November 2, 2026
Contact: Sample script for the Cold Open guide

EXT. HARBOR PARKING LOT - NIGHT

Rain on the windshield of a dented blue pickup truck. DANA REYES (30s, ferry mechanic, coffee in a thermos) sits behind the wheel, watching the last ferry load.

A TICKET AGENT waves a flashlight at the line of cars.

DANA
(to herself)
Twelve minutes. Plenty of time.

She grabs a canvas tool bag from the passenger seat and runs.

INT. FERRY - ENGINE ROOM - NIGHT

Hot, loud, dim. Pipes sweat. MILO OKAFOR (60s, chief engineer, reading glasses on a cord) taps a pressure gauge with a wrench.

MILO
You're late.

DANA
I'm early for tomorrow.

MILO
The port engine's been coughing since Seattle.

Dana kneels at the engine, opens her tool bag, pulls out a flashlight.

DANA
Hand me the torque wrench.

He does. Their hands touch the same tool for a beat too long.

EXT. FERRY - UPPER DECK - NIGHT

Wind. Rain. PASSENGERS huddle under the overhang. A GIRL (8) in a yellow raincoat presses her face to the railing.

Dana climbs the ladder, wiping grease off on her jeans. She spots the girl.

DANA
Where are your people?

GIRL
Inside. I wanted to see the lighthouse.

DANA
That's the lighthouse. Now you've seen it.

The lighthouse beam sweeps across them both.

INT. FERRY - PASSENGER CABIN - NIGHT

Rows of vinyl seats. A vending machine hums. CAPTAIN ROSA VEGA (50s, uniform, radio on her hip) walks the aisle.

CAPTAIN VEGA
(into radio)
Engine room, talk to me.

MILO (V.O.)
(over radio)
Dana's on it. Give us ten.

Captain Vega finds the girl's MOTHER asleep across three seats and gently shakes her.

INT. FERRY - ENGINE ROOM - CONTINUOUS

Dana tightens a fitting. The engine note smooths out.

MILO
Listen to that.

DANA
That's the sound of me getting paid.

Milo laughs, then coughs. He hides a pill bottle in his coat pocket. Dana sees it.

DANA (CONT'D)
Milo.

MILO
Not tonight.

EXT. ISLAND DOCK - DAWN

The ferry noses into the slip. Gulls. Dana walks off with her tool bag, Milo beside her. The girl waves from the deck in her yellow raincoat.

MILO
Same time tomorrow?

DANA
I'll bring the coffee.

FADE OUT.
